{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-descartes-knot-eigenbasis","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Corollary","doco:Section"],"label":"cor:descartes-knot-eigenbasis","kind":"corollary","title":"Knot eigenbasis completeness for a Descartes universe","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-descartes-braid-structure","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-jones-markov-trace","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-knot-eigenbasis-complete"],"tags":["archimedean-universe","knot-invariant","hecke-algebra","schur-weyl"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.descartes_knot_eigenbasis","text":"descartes-knot-eigenbasis.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"cor:descartes-knot-eigenbasis\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a Descartes universe (<a href=\"#def:archimedean-condition\">Descartes condition</a>) with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C} = \\mathrm{Rep}(\\mathrm{SU}_q(2))</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V</code> the fundamental representation. The knot-type eigenbasis of the algebraic direct limit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_{\\mathrm{phys}} = \\varinjlim V^{\\otimes n}</code> is complete.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes-knot-eigenbasis.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Corollary","number":"7.8.17"}
